# LaTeX build output, except the compiled PDFs themselves, which are committed
# on purpose so the book is readable without a LaTeX toolchain (see CLAUDE.md's
# "Compiling chapters" and "The subject index" sections). Regenerate these with
# pdflatex/makeindex rather than hand-editing them.
*.aux
*.toc
*.idx
*.ind
*.ilg
*.log
*.dvi
*.out

# Raw datasets downloaded by capstone-chapter notebooks (large binaries; the
# notebook re-downloads them automatically from their public source on demand).
ch16_data/

# Synthetic data generated by chapter notebooks' own simulation code (fully
# reproducible from the fixed random seed in the notebook; not downloaded from
# anywhere, so there is nothing to commit).
ch12_data/

# SyncTeX editor-sync byproducts (regenerated per-machine/editor; not build output anyone else needs).
*.synctex.gz

# Everything instructor-facing: the lecture slide decks and their build system, and
# the solutions to the chapter-end Suggested Exercises with their companion notebooks.
# None of this is manuscript content, and it stays local rather than going to the
# public repo. The whole directory is ignored, so material added under it later is
# covered without another rule.
# UNANCHORED on purpose. '/Instructors/' matched only the repo root, so after the
# 2026-08-05 move of the English content into en/ it stopped covering
# en/Instructors/ (444 files: slide decks, the build system, and the answer keys).
# A leading slash anchors a pattern to the .gitignore's own directory; a slash-free
# one matches at any depth and therefore survives a reorganisation.
Instructors/

# The two solutions rules below are now subsumed by /Instructors/ above, since the
# answer keys live at Instructors/Solutions_chapter_end_questions/. They are kept
# deliberately: they are unanchored, so they still catch these folders if they are
# ever moved back out of Instructors/ or created elsewhere in the tree.
solutions_chapter_end_questions/
solutions_chapter_end_questions_zh/

# The Chinese edition. It lives in its own PRIVATE repository, nested here as zh/ so
# that both editions stay editable in one working tree while being pushed to remotes
# of different visibility. This entry is the safety boundary: because zh/ is ignored,
# `git add -A` in this (public) repository cannot stage Chinese content, ever. Do not
# remove it. The Chinese build is run from inside zh/ (see CLAUDE.md).
/zh/

# Claude Code state and instructions. Never tracked or pushed, in either repository.
# .claude/ is listed explicitly because it happens to be empty right now, and git
# reports nothing for an empty directory: without this rule, the first file the tool
# writes there (settings.local.json, for instance) would show up as untracked and be
# swept in by `git add -A`.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

# Session transcripts, working notes, and editor workspace files: scratch, not manuscript.
session_log_*.txt
index_cleanup.md
vol_risk_premium_*
*.code-workspace

# Drafted material the author decided against including. Kept on disk so the
# work is not lost, deliberately unpublished. A draft that IS headed for the
# book (the draft_insurance.tex pattern) should be tracked instead of matched
# here, so add such files by exact name rather than widening this glob.
# UNANCHORED, for the same reason as Instructors/ above: 'chapters/...' contains a
# slash and so was anchored to the repo root, and stopped matching once the English
# content moved into en/. This is the abandoned production/MLOps appendix; it stays
# local and must never reach the public repository.
draft_appendix_production.*

# Local scratch, never part of either book. All four predate or postdate the
# en/ move and never had a rule; they surfaced as untracked once the layout
# settled. Unanchored so they stay ignored wherever they end up on disk.
frontmatter_extract*.tex
fix_watermark.py
inspect_watermark.py
update_watermark.py
